userStories.description:
**Goal** — Refuse git mutations that can delete, revert or stash .nax run state while preserving provably safe operands.

**Motivation** — The `.nax` guard allows `git rm -rf .nax`, `git reset -- .nax`, `--autostash` and `git sparse-checkout set src`.

**Approach** —
10. **Run-state guard gaps (#2551 item 3).** New logic lives in a new `nax-agent/src/tools/nax-verb-gaps.ts`, because `nax-state-guard.ts` is 491 of 600 lines. `verbRefusal` dispatches into it. Like every existing refusal, each new one applies only when a `.nax` directory is near the command's frames (`hasNaxDirNear` / `findNaxDirs`). An operand "touches `.nax`" by the existing `operandTouchesNax` (`nax-revert.ts`), which resolves it against the frames and, through `coversNax`, counts a directory that contains a `.nax` directory. The guard refuses:
    - a `git checkout`, `git restore`, `git rm` or `git reset` pathspec operand containing `*`, `?` or `[`, because a glob such as `'*.json'` can match files under `.nax`. An exclusion pathspec (`isExclusionSpec`, e.g. `':(top,exclude,glob)**/.nax/**'`, which the guard's own refusal text recommends) is exempt;
    - `git rebase`, `git pull` or `git merge` with `--autostash`;
    - `git rm` with any operand that touches `.nax`, whatever its flags (so `git rm -r .` and `git rm -r packages` refuse when they contain a `.nax` directory);
    - `git reset` with a path operand that touches `.nax`, whether before or after `--`;
    - `git sparse-checkout` with any subcommand other than `list`.

    `git stash push` without `--` is allowed when every path operand passes the same check as the `--` form (`pathIsClean`). Path operands are the tokens after `push` that do not start with `-`, skipping the value of `-m` / `--message`. `--pathspec-from-file` refuses, because its paths cannot be checked.

**Scope** — In: new nax-verb-gaps.ts dispatched by verbRefusal, exported existing helpers from nax-revert.ts/nax-stash-restore.ts, safe stash push parsing, and guard unit regressions. Out: US-003 canonical policy matching, US-007 reviewer repair and all ACP work. Restoring `.nax` files that `git sparse-checkout` already deleted; the guard now refuses the command. Applying `--autostash` refusal to `git -c rebase.autoStash=true` config overrides.

**Interface** — `coversNax(spec, ctx, nax)` and `splitOperands(verb, args)` (`nax-revert.ts`) and `pathIsClean(spec, ctx)` (`nax-stash-restore.ts`). Baseline: module-private. Target: exported unchanged, for `nax-verb-gaps.ts`; `coversNax`'s third argument is `findNaxDirs(ctx)`. Baseline clarification: operandTouchesNax alone does not recognize directory ancestors; the new refusal must also call coversNax to achieve the stated directory behavior without changing the helper contracts. Use existing locateGit/effective frames and exclusion checks; do not change the shared commandHeadIndex or bypass near-.nax gating. AC22 uses the top-anchored spelling ':(top,exclude,glob)**/.nax/**' (COVERING_EXCLUSION in nax-revert.ts), which the existing isCoveringExclusion already accepts; the only change is exempting exclusion pathspecs from the new glob refusal. The exclusion validators in nax-revert.ts are not changed. Stash allow cases use existing regular src/a.ts files, as the unchanged pathIsClean helper requires.
